{
 "id": "192-14",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "I want you to forget about the ticketing system entirely.",
  "We work closely and directly here, and I expect you to bring any issues, questions, or progress updates directly to me.",
  "It's important to maintain consistency and clarity in our code.",
  "So, when naming attributes, always start with 'q_'.",
  "For function argument names, use 'a_' as the prefix.",
  "This helps keep our code organized and readable.",
  "It's a convention I've found helpful in maintaining a clear distinction between attributes and arguments.",
  "It also prevents naming conflicts and makes our code more self-documenting.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you need any clarification along the way.",
  "I'll be here to guide and support you.",
  "When naming function arguments, always start the name with 'f_' as in 'f_argument'.",
  "This is to maintain consistency and improve code readability.",
  "It helps distinguish function arguments from other variables.\"",
  "\"Additionally, always add the '@validate' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all your functions.",
  "This enforces type-checking and helps catch potential errors early.",
  "It's an important part of our code review process.\"",
  "\"Consistency and maintainability.",
  "We have a large codebase, and these standards help ensure that our code is readable and less prone to errors."
 ],
